packets.implementation:
DESIGN (three options weighed). (a) Rewrite path calls in the parser into shapes the generic resolver already handles - REJECTED: the parser sees one file, and `crate::`, `super::`, a sibling crate's name and re-exports are cross-file facts. (b) Teach the shared resolve_attribute_target about `::` bases - REJECTED: it serves 16 languages and `::` bases also come from PHP/C++ static calls with other semantics. (c) A Rust-only resolver passed through the reserved extra_hook - CHOSEN: it runs only after generic resolution misses, so every edge that resolves on HEAD resolves identically, non-Rust graphs are byte-identical, and Rust graphs only gain edges.

NEW MODULE graph/src/rust_paths.rs (~270 LOC):
```rust
/// One Cargo package's crate roots, as the engine found them in the walk.
#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct RustCrate {
    /// Path identifier: the package name with `-` -> `_` (`repo-graph-engine` -> `repo_graph_engine`).
    pub name: String,
    /// Package dir as a qname prefix (`engine`; "" for a package at the repo root).
    pub dir: String,
    /// Module qname of the library root (`engine::src::lib`), when the package has one.
    pub lib_root: Option<String>,
    /// Every other crate root it owns: src/main.rs, src/bin/*.rs, src/bin/*/main.rs, tests/*.rs, examples/*.rs, benches/*.rs (module qnames).
    pub other_roots: Vec<String>,
}
pub(crate) struct RustIndex { /* OWNED copies: resolve_calls holds &mut RepoGraph while the hook runs */ }
impl RustIndex {
    pub(crate) fn build(g: &RepoGraph, crates: &[RustCrate]) -> Self;
    pub(crate) fn resolve_call(&self, g: &RepoGraph, site: &CallSite) -> Option<NodeId>; // the extra_hook body
    pub(crate) fn resolve_path(&self, g: &RepoGraph, from: NodeId, base: &str, name: &str) -> Option<NodeId>;
    pub(crate) fn report(&self);
}
```
Index contents (built once after build_symbol_table): module_by_qname (clone), module_symbols (clone), class_methods for STRUCT/CLASS plus METHOD children of ENUM/INTERFACE from nav.children_of (so `Enum::assoc()` resolves; LA.3 adds variants), `impl_elsewhere`: (type simple name, member) -> sorted Vec<NodeId> of METHODs whose nav parent is a MODULE (visit_impl parents a method to the module when the impl'd type lives in another file; its qname is `<module>::<Type>::<m>`), per-crate `crate_items`: top-level def name -> sorted Vec<NodeId> over every FILE MODULE (kind MODULE, never an inline-mod PACKAGE that LA.3 adds) whose qname starts with the crate's `<dir>::src::` prefix, and Cell<usize> counters (the hook is `Fn`).

resolve_path: split `base` on `::` after stripping a leading `::` and any `::<...>` turbofish segment; give up on a base starting with `<` (`<T as Trait>`). FIRST SEGMENT -> a start node: (1) `crate` -> the caller's crate root; (2) `self` -> the caller's enclosing module (nearest MODULE, or PACKAGE once LA.3 emits inline mods); (3) `super` (repeatable) -> PARENT; (4) `Self` -> the caller's enclosing STRUCT/ENUM/CLASS/INTERFACE by nav parents, or, for a method parented to a MODULE, the type segment of its own qname via impl_elsewhere; (5) a name in the caller module's module_import_bindings; (6) a child module of the caller module (file child or, after LA.3, an inline PACKAGE); (7) a type defined in the caller module (module_symbols -> STRUCT/ENUM/CLASS/INTERFACE); (8) a workspace crate name -> that crate's lib_root. Duplicate crate names (two bench fixtures may both call a package `acme-app`) -> the crate whose `dir` shares the longest `::`-segment prefix with the caller's module; a tie -> unresolved. REMAINING SEGMENTS: from a MODULE/PACKAGE the next segment is a child module (`<children-prefix>::<seg>`, `<children-prefix>::<seg>::mod`, or an inline PACKAGE child by name) or a type defined there; from a type only the final name may follow. FINAL NAME: in a module -> module_symbols[m][name], else m's own import bindings (this is what follows `pub use` re-exports once LA.1b parses them), else, ONLY when m is a crate root, the unique-in-crate fallback: exactly one top-level def named `name` in that crate's crate_items (ambiguous -> None). That fallback is what makes `repo_graph_engine::service_map` resolve while the facade's `pub use arch::{..}` is still unparsed. In a type -> class_methods/ENUM members, else impl_elsewhere for (type, name) unique within the caller's crate.
MODULE PATH of a file module m: m minus a trailing `mod` segment (`x::y::mod` -> `x::y`), else m. CHILDREN-PREFIX of m: m minus its last segment when that segment is `lib`/`main`/`mod` or m is a crate root; else m (Rust 2018 `a.rs` + `a/b.rs`). PARENT of a file module m: the module whose children-prefix equals m's MODULE PATH minus its last segment (`<p>`, `<p>::mod`, or the crate root `<p>::lib` / `<p>::main`); a crate root has none. (Using m itself instead of its module path would make `x/y/mod.rs` its own parent.) CRATE ROOT of m: m itself if m is in some other_roots; else the crate with the longest `dir` prefix whose `<dir>::src::` contains m -> its lib_root (else its `<dir>::src::main`); no covering crate (loose .rs files, e.g. fixtures/rust-axum-imports) -> walk up m's directory for a `<d>::lib` / `<d>::main` module; none -> the repo root is the crate dir (children-prefix ""), which is exactly HEAD's behaviour for loose files.
Only Attribute{base,name} call sites are examined; Bare/SelfMethod/SuperMethod/ComplexReceiver return None here (LA.3 adds enum self-calls, LA.1b adds scope-chain bindings). Everything is lookup-only: indexes are queried by key, every candidate list is sorted by qname before a tie-break, and no winner is ever picked by iterating a HashMap.

graph/src/build.rs:
```rust
pub fn build_rust(repo: RepoId, parses: Vec<FileParse>, crates: &[RustCrate]) -> Result<RepoGraph, GraphError> {
    let (mut g, all_imports, all_calls, all_refs) = merge_parses(repo, parses);
    build_symbol_table(&mut g);
    resolve_imports_python(&mut g, &all_imports); // unchanged until LA.1b
    let idx = RustIndex::build(&g, crates);
    resolve_calls(&mut g, &all_calls, |g, site| idx.resolve_call(g, site));
    resolve_refs(&mut g, &all_refs);
    idx.report();
    Ok(g)
}
```
FACADE (graph/src/lib.rs): `mod rust_paths;`, `pub use build::{build_dotted, build_go, build_python, build_ruby, build_rust, build_typescript};`, `pub use rust_paths::RustCrate;`.

ENGINE (engine/src/build.rs): `fn rust_crates(files: &[(String, String)], roots: &[ProjectRoot]) -> Vec<RustCrate>` - for each root with ecosystem "cargo": name = label.replace('-', "_"); dir = rel_path with `/` -> `::`; lib_root = path_to_qname("<rel>/src/lib.rs") when that file is in `files`; other_roots = every walked file matching `<rel>/src/main.rs`, `<rel>/src/bin/*.rs`, `<rel>/src/bin/*/main.rs`, `<rel>/tests/*.rs`, `<rel>/examples/*.rs`, `<rel>/benches/*.rs` (exact depth), as path_to_qname. A root with neither (a `[workspace]`-only manifest) is skipped. Result sorted by (dir, name). build_graphs_for_repo gains `roots: &[ProjectRoot]` and dispatches `"rust" => repo_graph_graph::build_rust(repo, parses, &rust_crates(files, roots))`; generate_one_inner and generate_many_inner pass `&roots`.

MARKER: RustIndex::report prints once per build_rust call when the hook examined >= 1 path call. P counts Attribute sites whose FIRST base segment resolved to a start node (crate/self/super/Self/import/child/type/crate_name - the per-rule counters, which sum to P); R counts those whose whole path resolved; a site like `e.run()` whose base names no start node is not a path call and is not counted: `[rust-paths] path calls resolved R/P (crate=a self=b super=c Self=d import=e child=f type=g crate_name=h unique_in_crate=i) crates=N`.

TESTS engine/tests/rust_crate_paths.rs (tempfile + generate_one): (1) `crate_paths_resolve` - the fixture shape below; assert each of the six CALLS edges by qname, the forbidden main -> app::src::main::helper edge absent, and `entrypoint_reachable(&merged)` contains core::src::api::service_map (live from app's `main`); (2) `duplicate_crate_names_bind_to_the_nearest_workspace` - ws1/{core,app} and ws2/{core,app} with identical package names, each app's `acme_core::api::helper()` binds into its own sibling core; (3) `loose_files_keep_head_behaviour` - `main.rs` + `util.rs` with no Cargo.toml and `crate::util::greet()` resolve as today.
CLAUDE.md: add `rust_paths.rs` to the graph/src line of the 'Module layout' block, and one sentence under 'Parser-vs-Graph Split' that Rust is the first language to use the extra_hook seam (graph/src/rust_paths.rs).

