DESIGN. (a) Fold services below N files/nodes - REJECTED (arbitrary; wrong both ways, see rationale). (b) Stop detecting host shells as PROJECT roots - REJECTED: `glia projects` and `--scope` legitimately name a Gradle build, and the PROJECT node is a fact about the manifest. (c) Fold in arch keying only, by a structural rule - CHOSEN.

engine/src/arch.rs (~70 LOC):
```rust
/// Native shells a cross-platform app framework generates inside the app (Flutter: all five; React Native / Capacitor / Tauri: android, ios).
const PLATFORM_HOST_DIRS: &[&str] = &["android", "ios", "macos", "linux", "windows"];
/// Ecosystems whose project owns such shells.
const HOST_OWNER_ECOSYSTEMS: &[&str] = &["dart", "npm"];
/// Ecosystems a shell's own build manifest uses.
const HOST_SHELL_ECOSYSTEMS: &[&str] = &["gradle", "cmake", "swift", "maven"];
/// host root path -> owning app root path, sorted.
fn platform_host_roots(merged: &MergedGraph) -> BTreeMap<String, String>;
```
Rule: a root R with ecosystem in HOST_SHELL_ECOSYSTEMS is a host of app A iff A is the NEAREST root with ecosystem in HOST_OWNER_ECOSYSTEMS whose path is a proper directory prefix of R (A may be the repo root `.`), and the first path component of R relative to A is in PLATFORM_HOST_DIRS. Nested shells fold transitively (mobile/android/app -> mobile, because its nearest owner-ecosystem ancestor is mobile and the component after `mobile/` is `android`). Input = crate::answers::project_roots(merged) (sorted by path), so the rule reads only PROJECT nodes and their ORIGIN cells and behaves identically on a fresh build and a loaded .gmap. project_root_paths drops every key of that map; default_keying runs on what remains, so a Flutter app at the repo ROOT whose only sub-roots were its shells now falls back to TopLevelDir - the same keying a plain single-root repo already gets. Service ids, link rows and the Dropped footer need no other change: a host's files now land in the app's bucket through service_of's longest prefix. tools/plugin (Gradle under an npm dir, but not in a platform dir) stays its own service - the precision half.
MARKER, printed only when >= 1 host folded: `[arch] platform hosts folded: N (mobile/android->mobile, mobile/android/app->mobile, ...)`, from service_map_with beside the existing `[arch]` line (whose format is unchanged - cli/tests/arch_cli.rs asserts it).
