PARSER (parsers/code/go/src/lib.rs, ~90 LOC):
```rust
/// Every go.mod in the repo: (module root as a qname prefix, module path). Sorted by root.
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Default, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct GoModules { mods: Vec<GoModule> }
#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct GoModule { pub root_qname: String, pub module_path: String }
impl GoModules {
    pub fn root_only(prefix: &str) -> Self;                         // HEAD semantics: one go.mod at the repo root
    pub fn from_entries(entries: Vec<(String, String)>) -> Self;     // (root rel dir with '/', module path); sorted, deduped
    pub fn context_key(&self) -> String;                             // "<root>=<module>;..." - the cache context
    pub fn is_empty(&self) -> bool;
    fn map_import(&self, package_qname: &str, import_path: &str) -> Option<String>;
}
pub fn parse_file_with_modules(source: &str, file_rel_path: &str, package_qname: &str, go: &GoModules, repo: RepoId) -> Result<FileParse, ParseError>;
pub fn parse_file(source, file_rel_path, package_qname, module_import_prefix: &str, repo) // = parse_file_with_modules(.., &GoModules::root_only(prefix), ..)
```
map_import: `prefix_of(m, p) = p == m.module_path || p.starts_with(&format!("{}/", m.module_path))` (the `/` boundary). (1) OWN module first: among modules whose root_qname is a segment-prefix of package_qname (root "" matches all), the longest; if prefix_of -> Some(join(root_qname, rel.replace('/', "::"))). (2) else any other repo module by longest module_path with prefix_of (a sibling module in a go.work / replace layout), ties broken by root_qname order -> Some(join(that root, rel)). (3) else None -> today's raw external form. A degenerate import equal to a module path with nothing after it keeps HEAD's `return` (no ImportStmt). record_import uses it; nothing else in the parser reads the prefix (verified: record_import is the only reader).
ENGINE (~70 LOC): engine/src/build.rs `fn go_modules_for(root: &Path, roots: &[ProjectRoot]) -> GoModules` - every root with ecosystem "go" (rel_path "" included): read `<root>/<rel>/go.mod` with the existing module-line parser (read_go_module_prefix, now taking the dir), skip a go.mod with no module line. Marker once per repo when >= 1 module: `[go-modules] N module roots (svc=example.com/svc svc-b=example.com/svc-b) repo=<label>` (>= 5 entries: the first 4 then `+K more`). validate_context gets `&go.context_key()`. build_graphs_for_repo / parse_repo_files thread `&GoModules`; route.rs calls `parse_one_with_go_modules`. engine/src/extract.rs: parse_one_with keeps its `go_module_prefix: &str` signature (pyo3 and external callers) and delegates with GoModules::root_only; `parse_one_with_go_modules` is new and public. FACADE: engine/src/lib.rs `pub use extract::{parse_one, parse_one_with, parse_one_with_go_modules};` and `pub use repo_graph_parser_go::GoModules;` so callers of the new fn can build the map.
engine/src/cache.rs: field `go_prefix` -> `go_modules` (doc: 'module-set key from GoModules::context_key; any go.mod added, removed or edited discards the cache'); validate_context's second parameter renamed `go_context`. The context key moves from a bare module path to `=module` form, so every existing sidecar discards once - the stamp changes on this commit anyway.
TESTS engine/tests/go_modules.rs (tempfile, ~70 LOC): `nested_go_mods_map_internal_imports` (the fixture shape: IMPORTS svc::cmd::main -> svc::internal::store::store, CALLS main -> svc::internal::store::store::Save, and no edge into svc-b::internal::store::store); `imports_cell_lists_only_third_party` (main's IMPORTS cell == ["github.com/google/uuid"] exactly); `prefix_boundary` (module example.com/svc never claims example.com/svc-b/... - unit test on GoModules::map_import in the parser crate as well); `editing_a_nested_go_mod_discards_the_cache` (generate_one_with_cache, change svc-b/go.mod's module line and the import in main.go's sibling, rebuild: the new mapping is used and the cache reports the context change).

