FACADE change (engine/src/lib.rs `mod pages;` + one `pub use`).
engine/src/pages.rs (~170 LOC incl. tests):
```rust
#[derive(serde::Serialize)] pub struct PageRecord { pub path: String, pub route_qname: String, pub handler: Option<String>, pub handler_file: Option<String>, pub handler_line: Option<i64>, pub redirect_to: Option<String>, pub catchall: bool, pub inbound_links: usize }
#[derive(serde::Serialize)] pub struct NavLinkRecord { pub from_qname: String, pub from_file: Option<String>, pub from_line: Option<i64>, pub to_path: String, pub confidence: &'static str }
#[derive(serde::Serialize)] pub struct DeadLink { pub from_qname: String, pub from_file: Option<String>, pub from_line: Option<i64>, pub link: String, pub absorbed_by: Option<String> /* catch-all path + its redirect, e.g. "/** -> /login" */ }
#[derive(serde::Serialize)] pub struct PageFlow { pub pages: Vec<PageRecord>, pub links: Vec<NavLinkRecord>, pub dead: Vec<DeadLink>, pub unlinked: Vec<String> }
pub fn page_flow(merged: &MergedGraph) -> PageFlow;
```
PAGES = every ROUTE for which `repo_graph_graph::is_nav_route(&cells)` holds (LA.6a export), its `path` from `repo_graph_graph::nav_route_path(qname)`, with its HANDLED_BY target (located via `crate::answers::locate_node`, already pub) and outgoing NAVIGATES_TO as `redirect_to`. LINKS = every NAVIGATES_TO edge whose source is not a ROUTE (redirects are shown on the page). DEAD = every NAVIGATES_TO entry in each graph's `unresolved_refs` whose `from` is a graph node, located, with `absorbed_by` set when that graph has a catch-all nav route. UNLINKED = nav routes with zero inbound NAVIGATES_TO that are not `/` and not a ROOT catch-all (a scoped catch-all such as `/docs/:slug*` is a page and can be unlinked) - reported as a FACT ("no in-repo link reaches this page"), never called dead (email / external deep links exist). All four lists sorted by (path | from_qname, link) for determinism; line numbers use whatever convention `locate_node` has when this lands (LD.1 owns the 1-based switch).
CLI `glia pages <repo> [--with <repo>]... [--dead-only] [--json]` (cli/src/main.rs, ~70 LOC): builds like `cmd_contracts`, prints `# glia pages <repo>` then a pages table (path, handler, file:line, inbound), a links table, a DEAD section (`<from> -> <link>  (absorbed by /** -> /login)`), an UNLINKED list; `--dead-only` prints only DEAD; `--json` prints the PageFlow. Exit code 0 even with dead links (report, not gate).
pyo3 (py/src/lib.rs, ~25 LOC): `fn page_flow_json(merged: &MergedGraph) -> Result<String, serde_json::Error>` printing `[pages] surface=pyo3 repos=N`, and `PyGraph::page_flow` returning the JSON string, matching `contracts()` (LD.2 later decides JSON-string vs native for every method at once).
coverage.rs `COVERAGE_CAVEATS` row: `CoverageCaveat { language: "typescript", edge_category: "NAVIGATES_TO", note: "navigations built from variables (navigate([path]), navigateByUrl(url), router.push(url)), Vue named-route pushes and Angular relative navigations are not resolved; lazily loaded child tables in another file match only by path suffix (Weak)", verify: "grep -rnE 'navigate\\(|navigateByUrl|router\\.push|routerLink' src" }`.
MARKER, both surfaces: `[pages] surface=<cli|pyo3> repos=N pages=P links=L dead=D unlinked=U`.
engine/tests/page_flow.rs: tempdir Angular app mirroring LA.6c's nav-angular-links fixture (route table with `**` -> /login and no `connect`; profile.component.ts with the origin share link; home template linking /home) -> `generate_one` -> `page_flow(&merged)`: `dead.len() == 1`, `dead[0].link == "/connect"`, `dead[0].from_qname` ends with `ProfileComponent`, `dead[0].absorbed_by == Some("/** -> /login")`; `pages` contains `/home` with handler ending `HomeComponent`; `unlinked == vec!["/profile"]` exactly (routes home, login, verify-email, profile, user/:publicId, **: /home and /user/:publicId are linked from the template, /home and /verify-email from LoginComponent, /login by the `**` redirect edge, the catch-all is excluded); JSON round-trip through `page_flow_json` parses and has the four keys.

