```
The body hash is an inline FNV-1a 64 (the stamp/build.rs precedent): graph has no hashing dependency and a stored hint must hash identically across toolchains, which rules out std's DefaultHasher; no Cargo.toml / Cargo.lock change.
identity_of: kind from nav; walk parent_of up to the first MODULE (bounded by nav depth), collecting names; file = basename of the POSITION `file` (the node's own POSITION first, else its MODULE's); body from the node's CODE cell (MODULE CODE = the whole file for the parsers that attach it, which makes file-level exact moves free).
rebind (the LF / Engram path): exact (kind?, qname) unique -> Exact; else parse the hint and try (kind, file, local) unique -> Moved{SameName}; else (kind, body) unique with body != 0 -> Moved{Identical}; several -> Ambiguous (sorted ids); none -> Orphan. Evidence tier HEURISTIC for Moved, documented on the enum; callers report it, never silently apply Ambiguous.
detect_moves_with (the LE.1 / LG.8 path; pure, deterministic): removed MODULEs = in prior, absent from current by (repo, kind, qname) - RepoIds are stable after LB.1, so repo is part of the key; added = the converse. Pair files in three passes, each requiring a UNIQUE partner on both sides: (0) a declared (old_path, new_path) whose old path owns a removed MODULE and whose new path owns an added one -> Declared (FACT: the caller's VCS said so); (1) equal MODULE body hash -> Identical (pure moves and pure renames); (2) equal basename + extension -> SameName, accepted only if at least half (and >= 1) of the old file's descendant (kind, local) keys also exist under the new MODULE - otherwise counted `rejected` (an unrelated new users.py must not inherit the old one's identity). Within each accepted file move the MODULE pair is a NodeMove (local "") and descendants align by (kind, local) -> NodeMove; unaligned descendants stay plain removed/added. Output sorted by old_path and by (old_qname, kind). carry_file_tokens: every current file gets prior[old_path] when it is the new_path of a FileMove, prior[path] when it existed before, else its own path (the token of a never-moved file is its path at first sight - LG.9's contract). Marker once per detect call. Not handled (documented): a file moved AND renamed AND edited without a declared rename; a symbol renamed inside a moved file (delete + add); MODULE qname collisions across languages in one dir (see gaps).
graph/tests/identity_moves.rs (~130 LOC): hand-built graphs: hint round-trip; rebind tiers incl. Ambiguous for two `index.ts` modules with the same local path; detect_moves on synthetic prior/current; a declared rename wins over a basename match; carry_file_tokens keeps the first-sight token across two successive moves. engine/tests/identity_moves.rs (~80 LOC): real builds, see acceptance.

