```rust
impl MergedGraph {
  /// One-hop neighbours of `id` over intra AND cross edges, in global edge order (graphs in Vec order, then cross_edges).
  /// `follow = None` = every category. Forward = outgoing, Backward = incoming, Both = both (a self-loop once, as Forward).
  pub fn neighbours(&self, id: NodeId, reach: Reach, follow: Option<&[EdgeCategoryId]>) -> Vec<(NodeId, EdgeCategoryId, Reach)>;
  /// BFS from `seeds` (seeds excluded) - algo::reach::bfs over Adjacency::build(self, &CategorySet::of(f) | all()). Discovery order.
  pub fn bfs(&self, seeds: &[NodeId], reach: Reach, follow: Option<&[EdgeCategoryId]>, max_depth: usize) -> Vec<Reached>;
  pub fn predecessors(&self, sink: NodeId, follow: Option<&[EdgeCategoryId]>, max_depth: usize) -> Vec<NodeId>;   // bfs Backward ids
  pub fn reachable_by(&self, sink: NodeId, sources: &[NodeId], follow: Option<&[EdgeCategoryId]>, max_depth: usize) -> Vec<NodeId>; // algo::reach::reachable_by, `sources` order
  /// Shortest path by hop count; `None` if unreachable within max_depth. Each step = (node, category of the edge that entered it; None for `from`).
  pub fn shortest_path(&self, from: NodeId, to: NodeId, reach: Reach, follow: Option<&[EdgeCategoryId]>, max_depth: usize) -> Option<Vec<(NodeId, Option<EdgeCategoryId>)>>;
}
```
neighbours is a single linear scan of all_edges (a one-node query does not justify building an index). bfs / predecessors / reachable_by / shortest_path build one Adjacency per call and delegate to algo::reach; shortest_path runs bfs(&[from]) and walks `Reached.parent` back from `to` (parents are recorded at first discovery, so the path is a shortest one and deterministic: ties break by global edge order, LD.15a parity rule 2); from == to -> Some(vec![(from, None)]). Reach -> Walk mapping Forward/Backward/Both (same crate, so Reach's #[non_exhaustive] from LD.9 does not bite). RepoGraph::neighbours gains the same `reach` parameter and return shape for symmetry. Marker, one line per bfs / predecessors / reachable_by / shortest_path call on a MergedGraph (NOT neighbours - the wrapper calls it per node and a line per call would flood): `eprintln!("[traverse] op={op} walk={walk:?} seeds={} reached={} index_nodes={}", ..)`.

