Parser (extraction only): interface method_elem -> METHOD node with qname `<interface qname>::<method name>`, nav parent = the INTERFACE, a DEFINES edge, POSITION + CODE via the existing entity_cells(). A6.6's build_symbol_table INTERFACE arm then files them in interface_methods (never class_methods, so unique_global_method's Go HANDLED_BY fallback is unaffected - A6.6's own guard). type_elem whose child is a single type_identifier (an embedded interface; unions / `~T` constraints are skipped) -> UnresolvedRef { from: interface id, qualifier: Bare(name), category: INHERITS_FROM } resolved by resolve_refs' existing global fallback.
Graph (resolution) - graph/src/build.rs:
```rust
/// Go satisfies interfaces implicitly: a named type implements an interface when its method NAME set covers the
/// interface's (own + embedded, transitively). Signatures are not compared (the parser records none) - hence Medium.
fn emit_go_implicit_implements(g: &mut RepoGraph)
```
method_set(iface) = interface_methods[iface] names ∪ method_set of each INHERITS_FROM target that is an INTERFACE (DFS with a visited set: cycle-safe). Skip interfaces whose full set is empty (`interface{}`, pure constraint interfaces). For every STRUCT (and CLASS, for named non-struct types if the parser ever records them) with class_methods: if the type's method names ⊇ method_set(iface), push IMPLEMENTS type -> iface at Confidence::Medium, unless an IMPLEMENTS edge between them already exists. Collect pairs into a Vec, sort by (from.0, to.0), dedup, then push - class_methods / interface_methods are HashMaps with a per-process seed and edge order feeds shard hashes (byte_identical). A6.6's method-level pass runs AFTER this, so MemStore::Get -> Store::Get IMPLEMENTS follow for free. Pointer vs value receivers are not distinguished (both count toward the type's set) - documented in the LD.7c go IMPLEMENTS caveat row. Marker: `eprintln!("[iface] go implicit implements: {} (interfaces={} types={} embedded={})")` when any interface exists.

