```rust
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, PartialOrd, Ord)]
pub enum Stage { Resolve, Post, Finalize }            // run order; Finalize = canonicalisation (the determinism sort)
pub struct PassSpec<G: 'static, C: 'static = ()> {
    pub name: &'static str,
    pub stage: Stage,
    pub after: &'static [&'static str],      // asserted, never solved
    pub populates: &'static [CellTypeId],    // node cell types this pass writes; verified both ways by the domain's test
    pub run: fn(&mut G, &C),
}   // manual Clone/Copy impls: derive would demand G: Clone, C: Clone
pub struct PassRegistry<G: 'static, C: 'static = ()> { specs: &'static [PassSpec<G, C>] }
impl<G, C> PassRegistry<G, C> {
    pub const fn new(specs: &'static [PassSpec<G, C>]) -> Self;
    pub const fn empty() -> Self;
    pub fn specs(&self) -> &'static [PassSpec<G, C>];
    pub fn order(&self) -> Vec<&'static PassSpec<G, C>>;  // stable sort by stage; declaration order within a stage
    pub fn validate(&self) -> Result<(), Vec<String>>;    // unique non-empty names; every `after` name exists AND precedes this pass in order()
    pub fn run(&self, g: &mut G, ctx: &C) -> PassReport;  // order() sequentially; no printing (the caller owns the marker)
}
#[derive(Clone, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq)] pub struct PassReport { pub ran: Vec<&'static str>, pub resolve: usize, pub post: usize, pub finalize: usize }
```
DESIGN CHOICES. (a) fn pointers in a &'static slice, not Vec<Box<dyn Pass>>: the registry is data (deterministic order, zero allocation, const-constructible so a domain declares it as a const); passes hold no state. (b) Stage instead of free ordering: a pass appended later can never run after the determinism sort by accident. (c) `after` is validated, not topologically solved: order is declaration order, and a solver would let a mis-declared list silently reorder existing passes. (d) Only ONE capability is declared - `populates` (cell types) - because LD.14's cell_populators() reads it; edge categories a pass emits are NOT declared (no consumer; LC.3 evidence records the emitter per edge; memory 'derive capability tables, don't write them'), and the declared list is proven by the populates_is_exact test. (e) C is the domain's build context (see rationale); code uses C = () until an LF stage lands. (f) Generic over G so LD.16's toy graph reuses it; activation stays free of MergedGraph.

