natspec.rs (~120 LOC). No serde derive: engram-export has no direct serde dependency (Cargo.toml: bincode, serde_json, clap), so the cell is read through serde_json::Value exactly like origin_provenance (lib.rs:92).
```rust
pub struct Tag { pub tag: String, pub name: Option<String>, pub text: String }
/// LA.8's DOC_TAGS cell (cell_type::DOC_TAGS), only when style == "natspec".
pub fn tags_of(cells: &[Cell]) -> Option<Vec<Tag>>;
pub struct TagFact { pub suffix: String, pub text: String }
pub struct Mapped { pub doc: Option<String>, pub facts: Vec<TagFact>, pub inheritdoc: Vec<String> }
pub fn map(symbol_name: &str, tags: &[Tag]) -> Mapped;
```
MAPPING (NatSpec: untagged text is @notice, which LA.8 already applies):
- notice tags -> doc = their texts joined by one space, through clean_and_cap_doc. No notice -> the first title tag becomes the doc and emits no title fact. Neither -> doc None: the collapsed DOC text is never used for a symbol that has a natspec DOC_TAGS cell (it would repeat every tag).
- inheritdoc tags -> base names (the tag's name, else the first word of its text); no fact.
- every other tag t (title, author, dev, param, return, custom:<x>, anything else LA.8 emits) -> suffix `natspec:<t>` + `:<name>` when name is Some; a suffix already used by this symbol gets `:<n>` appended (n = 1, 2, ... in source order), so two @dev lines give `natspec:dev` and `natspec:dev:1`; text `<symbol_name> @<t>[ <name>]: <text>`. The symbol name in the text keeps identical tag prose on two functions ('amount: The amount in wei') from collapsing onto one Engram content_key.
EMISSION in build_gmap: each TagFact becomes `GmapNode { key: format!("{symbol_key}#{suffix}"), content: Content::Proposition { text, span: Some(<the symbol's SpanRef>) }, provenance: Some("natspec".into()), concept_hint: <the symbol's>, identity_hint: <the symbol's hint>.map(|h| format!("{h}#{suffix}")) }`, pushed right after its symbol (deterministic: node order, then tag source order), plus `GmapEdge { from: <fact key>, kind: EdgeKind::Documents, to: symbol_key, weight: Some(1.0) }` - weight 1.0 because a tag is the symbol's own documentation (definitional, like Contains), unlike a README section's 0.3. Fact keys join seen_keys. Tag edges and inheritdoc edges are appended after the glia edge pass, in node order.
@inheritdoc <Base>: walk nav parent_of from the symbol to its parent CLASS / INTERFACE P; among P's outgoing INHERITS_FROM / IMPLEMENTS edges take the target whose qname's last segment == Base; else the unique exported CLASS / INTERFACE whose short name == Base; then, if `<base contract key>::<symbol name>` was exported, emit `GmapEdge { from: <base function key>, kind: Documents, to: symbol_key, weight: Some(1.0) }` and count it resolved; otherwise count it unresolved (no edge).
Symbols without a natspec DOC_TAGS cell - every other language - keep the DOC-cell path unchanged.
MARKER: `[engram-export] v6 natspec: {facts} tag facts + {edges} Documents edges on {symbols} symbols (inheritdoc {resolved}/{resolved+unresolved} resolved)` - edges counts tag edges plus inheritdoc edges.
TEST engram-export/tests/natspec_v6.rs (~130 LOC; temp dir + generate_one + build_gmap): contracts/IVault.sol (`interface IVault { /// @notice Withdraw funds.\n function withdraw(uint256 amount) external; }`) and contracts/Vault.sol: `contract Vault is IVault` under a block `/// @title A simple vault` / `/// @notice Holds deposits for users` / `/// @dev Uses a mapping for balances` / `/// @dev Owner-free`; deposit under `@notice Deposit ether into the vault` / `@dev Emits no event` / `@param who The account credited` / `@return credited The new balance` over `function deposit(address who) public payable returns (uint256 credited)`; withdraw under `/// @inheritdoc IVault` / `/// @author Someone` over `function withdraw(uint256 amount) external {}`; plus svc/orders.py. Exact assertions: deposit doc == 'Deposit ether into the vault'; facts `contracts::Vault::Vault::deposit#natspec:dev` = 'deposit @dev: Emits no event', `#natspec:param:who` = 'deposit @param who: The account credited', `#natspec:return:credited` = 'deposit @return credited: The new balance', each with provenance natspec, span == deposit's SpanRef and one Documents edge to deposit with weight Some(1.0); contract Vault doc == 'Holds deposits for users' with facts `#natspec:title` ('Vault @title: A simple vault'), `#natspec:dev` and `#natspec:dev:1`; withdraw has fact `#natspec:author` = 'withdraw @author: Someone' and doc None; exactly one Documents edge `contracts::IVault::IVault::withdraw` -> `contracts::Vault::Vault::withdraw`; stats natspec_symbols 4 (Vault, deposit, withdraw, IVault.withdraw), natspec_facts 7, natspec_edges 8, inheritdoc 1/1; the svc/orders.py nodes' content is byte-identical to an export of the same tree without the two .sol files.

