New signature `fn visit_children(node, src, file_rel, parent_qname: &str, type_scope: &str, parent_id, repo, acc)`. Root call: parent_qname = module_qname, type_scope = type_scope(module_qname). visit_namespace's body walk: `visit_children(body, src, file_rel, &qname, &qname, ns_id, repo, acc)` - braced types unchanged. The class / interface / enum arms call `visit_class(child, src, file_rel, type_scope, parent_id, repo, acc)` (same for interface / enum); inside, `let qname = scoped(scope, name);`. Nav parents and DEFINES edges are untouched (statement-form and namespace-less types stay MODULE children; braced ones PACKAGE children). trait_declaration is not visited at HEAD and stays so. Route passes: scan_laravel_routes (:749) / scan_slim_routes (:859) take module_id and Bare handler qualifiers, and Symfony attribute routes are emitted from the method id inside visit_class, so HANDLED_BY follows the new ids automatically (php-laravel-handled_by is the guard). Import resolution is unaffected: a `use App\Models\User` misses module_by_qname by path and binds through the tail fallback (unique_global_function by name, graph/src/imports.rs resolve_imports_python), which is qname-agnostic.
