parsers/code/csharp/src/lib.rs (~40 LOC non-test). Private `type_scope` / `scoped` as LB.7a; `fn has_modifier(node: TsNode, src: &[u8], word: &str) -> bool` scans node.children for kind `modifier` whose text == word. visit_children:
```rust
let at_root = node.kind() == "compilation_unit";
// LB.7d: a top-level type is scoped by the file-scoped namespace declared above it, else by the
// directory - never by the file stem. Below the root (block-namespace bodies) parent_qname is the
// namespace and nothing changes.
let mut type_scope: String = if at_root { type_scope(parent_qname).to_string() } else { parent_qname.to_string() };
...
"file_scoped_namespace_declaration" => { if let Some(ns) = visit_namespace(..) { if at_root { type_scope = ns; } } }
"namespace_declaration" => { visit_namespace(..); }
<type arms> => { let scope = if at_root && has_modifier(child, src, "file") { parent_qname } else { type_scope.as_str() };
                 visit_type_decl(child, src, file_rel, scope, parent_id, module_id, repo, acc); }
```
Parent structure is deliberately unchanged: file-scoped and namespace-less types stay MODULE children (DEFINES MODULE -> CLASS, exactly HEAD), so SharedSchemaResolver's MODULE-children walk still sees them - only qnames move. Partial classes split across files under one file-scoped or no namespace now share one qname and one NodeId (merge_parses folds them, as the block form already does). global_statement (minimal API) handling, collect_using and every route / DI / field-type pass (they take ids and Bare names; A6.2a keys field types by owner class id) are unchanged. A C# 11 `file` type keeps today's qname in every form.
