```rust
/// LB.9b: which code files name their MODULE by the full file name. A path_to_qname key claimed by
/// language-parser files of >= 2 build groups qualifies EVERY file of that key. A pure function of the
/// walked file list (BTree only), so parse, rpc needles and a warm cache all agree.
pub(crate) struct ModuleQnames { qualified: BTreeSet<String>, stems: usize, same_group_dupes: usize }
impl ModuleQnames {
    pub(crate) fn plan(files: &[(String, String)]) -> Self;   // BTreeMap<String /*bare*/, BTreeMap<&str /*group*/, Vec<&str /*path*/>>>
    pub(crate) fn module_qname(&self, path: &str) -> String;  // qualified: `<dir>::<file name>`, else path_to_qname(path)
    pub(crate) fn is_qualified(&self, path: &str) -> bool;
    pub(crate) fn module_id(&self, path: &str, repo: RepoId) -> NodeId; // NodeId::from_parts(GRAPH_TYPE, repo, MODULE, &self.module_qname(path))
}
```
`same_group_dupes` counts qualified keys where one group holds >= 2 files (util.js + util.ts + util.py): their alias is ambiguous and is not registered. Marker after the loop when qualified is non-empty: `[modules] cross-language stems: files={f} stems={s} same-group-ambiguous={a} repo={repo_label}`. Cache: ParseCache::get/put are unchanged (no cache.rs edit, no public-API break); route.rs filters the hit with `fp.nodes.first().and_then(|n| fp.nav.qname_by_id.get(&n.id)) == Some(&planned)`, so a sibling appearing or vanishing reparses exactly the affected files.
code-domain/src/lib.rs (~30 LOC):
```rust
/// LB.9b: a code MODULE named by its full file name (`api::user.py`) keeps its stem as nav name
/// (`user`). Returns the stem-form qname (`api::user`) for such a MODULE, None for every other qname
/// (a normal module's last segment IS its name; a non-code MODULE's name is its whole file name, LB.9a).
pub fn bare_module_qname(qname: &str, name: &str) -> Option<String> {
    let (dir, last) = qname.rsplit_once("::").map_or(("", qname), |(d, l)| (d, l));
    let ext = last.strip_prefix(name)?.strip_prefix('.')?;
    if ext.is_empty() || ext.contains(['.', ':']) { return None; }
    Some(if dir.is_empty() { name.to_string() } else { format!("{dir}::{name}") })
}
```
