packets.implementation:
Split the resolver extractor into its SDL half and its code half.
(1) `pub fn extract_graphql_sdl_file_nodes(source: &str, module_id: NodeId, repo: RepoId) -> GraphqlNodes` - WHOLE-FILE mode for a routed .graphql / .gql file: sdl_resolvers(source, 0) over the whole text, no decorator patterns (they are code). engine/src/route.rs's graphql branch calls it. On real SDL this equals HEAD's output (decorator patterns never match SDL): route.rs's graphql_schema_files_route_to_the_sdl_scan (Query + getUser with their POSITION rows) and graphql_operation_documents_mint_nothing are the guards.
(2) extract_graphql_resolver_nodes - CODE mode, same signature, still called by engine/src/extract.rs: DECORATOR_PATTERNS (@Query( @Mutation( @Subscription( @Resolver( @ResolveField( @strawberry.type @strawberry.mutation ObjectType): graphene.ObjectType) and the decorator-method scan exactly as today; SDL only as `for (start, end) in gql_literal_regions(source) { names.extend(sdl_resolvers(&source[start..end], line_of(source, start))) }`.
(3) `fn sdl_resolvers(text: &str, base_line: u32) -> Vec<(String, u32)>`: the SDL block scan lifted from extract_resolver_field_names (in_sdl_type + sdl_field_name, unchanged) plus the ROOT noun: a line whose trimmed text starts with a SDL_RESOLVER_TYPES entry, or `extend ` + one, yields the root name at that line. The whole-file `find` anywhere is gone, so a root opener in the middle of a line (a comment, a one-line string) never counts. Lines count from base_line, so anchors stay source lines.
(4) `fn gql_literal_regions(source: &str) -> Vec<(usize, usize)>` - literal BODIES, sorted by start and deduplicated, every bound on an ASCII delimiter (slicing is char-safe); an opener must be preceded by a non-identifier byte:
   tags: "gql`", "graphql`" -> body to the next unescaped backtick;
   magic comment: `/* GraphQL */` + optional whitespace + a literal;
   calls: `gql(`, `graphql(`, `buildSchema(`, `MustParseSchema(`, `ParseSchema(`, `from_definition(` (graphql-ruby) + optional whitespace + a literal;
   assignments: the identifier `typeDefs` or `type_defs`, an optional `: <type>` annotation, `=` or `:`, whitespace, an optional `/* ... */`, then a literal (a gql / graphql tag or call there is caught by the rules above);
   heredocs: `<<~GRAPHQL`, `<<-GRAPHQL`, `<<GRAPHQL` and the same with GQL -> body to the line whose trimmed text equals the delimiter;
   leading magic comment: any backtick or triple-quoted literal whose body starts (after whitespace) with `#graphql` or `# graphql` - the Apollo Server 4 convention `const typeDefs = ` + backtick + `#graphql` (an SDL comment line, so sdl_resolvers skips it).
   Literal openers: backtick (to the next unescaped backtick, multi-line), `"""` / `'''` (to the matching triple), `"` / `'` (to the next unescaped same quote on the same line). An unterminated literal yields no region.
(5) MARKER via LA.26's graphql_debug(): per code file with a region or an unmarked root opener, `[graphql-sdl-code] literals={n} roots={Query,..} fields={m} unmarked_roots={u}` where u counts root-type openers found outside every region (what HEAD would have minted from). The always-on route.rs `[graphql-sdl] files= resolvers=` line is unchanged.
TESTS (graphql.rs). Moved to whole-file mode (declared): detects_schema_type and extracts_sdl_type_field_names call extract_graphql_sdl_file_nodes (their input is a bare SDL document). Unchanged: anchors_resolvers_at_the_method_and_sdl_lines (its SDL is `const typeDefs = ` + backtick template, an assignment opener, so Query / getUser / listUsers stay at lines 1 / 2 / 3), extracts_decorator_method_field_name, detects_resolver_decorator, method_name_skips_modifiers. New: sdl_in_a_rust_comment_mints_nothing (route.rs:280's comment verbatim), sdl_in_an_unmarked_string_mints_nothing (`let sdl = "type Query {\n  getUser(id: ID!): User\n}\n";` and a multi-line Rust raw string holding `type Subscription {\n  orderShipped: Order\n}`), sdl_in_a_python_comment_mints_nothing, gql_tagged_sdl_mints_root_and_fields (anchor lines asserted), ariadne_gql_call_mints_fields, go_must_parse_schema_literal_mints_fields, ruby_graphql_heredoc_mints_fields, graphql_magic_comment_template_mints_fields, hash_graphql_template_mints_fields (`const schema = ` + backtick + `#graphql\n  type Query {\n    books: [Book]\n  }\n` + backtick -> Query + books, a variable name no assignment rule knows), sdl_file_mode_scans_the_whole_file.
