DESIGN (weighed): (a) a per-language hook for each enum-bearing language - REJECTED: Java, Swift, Dart and PHP have no hook, and the rule 'an enum owns its methods' is language-neutral; (b) widen the three generic lookups to ENUM - CHOSEN: an ENUM is a type that owns METHOD children in every parser that emits them (Rust same-file impl, Swift, and Java / TS after LA.30b / LA.30c). Only resolution that misses on HEAD can change: a SelfMethod whose enclosing type is an ENUM, an Attribute call whose bound base is an ENUM, and a USES Attribute ref whose base is an ENUM - none of which resolves today.
graph/src/calls.rs (~45 LOC):
```rust
/// Walk parents to the enclosing CLASS, STRUCT or ENUM (a type that owns methods).
fn enclosing_class_or_struct(nav: &CodeNav, start: NodeId) -> Option<NodeId> {
    // same loop; accept k == CLASS || k == STRUCT || k == ENUM
}
/// `Enum.MEMBER` / `Enum::Variant`: the ATTRIBUTE child of `enum_id` named `name`. Children are a Vec in record
/// order; two same-named ATTRIBUTE children (never emitted by one parser) -> None, never first-wins.
fn enum_member(g: &RepoGraph, enum_id: NodeId, name: &str) -> Option<NodeId>
```
resolve_attribute_target: `Some(k) if k == CLASS || k == STRUCT || k == ENUM => class_methods lookup`. resolve_refs Attribute arm: before the HANDLED_BY fallback, `if r.category == edge_category::USES` and `bindings[base]` is an ENUM, `enum_member(g, base_id, name)`; the ENUM-member lookup is USES-only, so a CALLS site `Color.RED()` can never bind to an ATTRIBUTE. unique_global_method: iterate class_methods but skip owners whose nav kind is ENUM (HANDLED_BY's global fallback keeps exactly the HEAD candidate set - no route handler binding can become ambiguous because an enum happens to own a same-named method).
graph/src/build.rs build_symbol_table (~3 LOC): `parent_kind == Some(CLASS) || Some(STRUCT) || Some(ENUM)` for the class_methods arm. The ATTRIBUTE children of an ENUM are NOT indexed there (class_methods is methods only).
MARKERS (graph, once per per-language build, only when non-zero; `ext` is the file extension of the POSITION cell of the lowest-qname ENUM that received a hit - the per-language discriminator, since resolve_calls does not know its language): resolve_calls prints `[resolve] enum-owned calls bound: self_method=S attribute=A ext=<ext>`; resolve_refs prints `[resolve] enum member uses bound: U ext=<ext>`. The ENUM is found through enclosing_class_or_struct / the bound base id; its file is read with one scan of g.nodes at print time.
TESTS graph/src/calls.rs mod tests (hand-built FileParses + build_dotted, the attribute_call_binds_package_base precedent): enum_self_method_resolves_against_the_enum (ENUM E, METHODs a / b, SelfMethod(b) from a -> exactly one CALLS a->b); self_method_through_an_attribute_parent_reaches_the_enum (METHOD m under ATTRIBUTE E::X under ENUM E, SelfMethod(b) -> E::b); attribute_call_binds_enum_base (m1 imports Symbol{module m2, name E}; Attribute{E, pick} -> CALLS to m2::E::pick); uses_ref_binds_enum_member (UnresolvedRef USES Attribute{E, RED} -> USES to ATTRIBUTE m2::E::RED, unresolved_refs empty); uses_ref_on_a_class_base_stays_unresolved (CLASS C with an ATTRIBUTE child X: USES Attribute{C, X} -> no edge, one unresolved_ref); calls_ref_never_binds_an_enum_member (CallSite Attribute{E, RED} -> no edge); enum_methods_stay_out_of_the_handled_by_global_pool (a HANDLED_BY ref Attribute{h, run} with one CLASS method run and one ENUM method run binds the CLASS method, exactly as HEAD with the ENUM absent). engine/tests/enum_owned_methods.rs: generate_one over bench/substrate-gap/fixtures/enum-owned-methods (read via CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR/../bench, the scope_filter.rs precedent): CALLS src::lib::Tier::rank -> src::lib::Tier::weight present, Ledger::total -> Ledger::weight present, the two forbids absent.
