struct Scope { parent_qname: String, parent_id: NodeId, ns_path: String /* named namespaces, "::"-joined; "" = global */ }
fn join(a: &str, b: &str) -> String { if a.is_empty() { b.to_string() } else { format!("{a}::{b}") } }
/// LB.10b: a header's type is named by its C++ name, a source file's by its file.
fn type_qname(acc: &Acc, scope: &Scope, name: &str) -> String {
    if !acc.is_header { join(&scope.parent_qname, name) }          // TU-local: HEAD's shape
    else if !scope.ns_path.is_empty() { join(&scope.ns_path, name) } // `shop::Cart`
    else { join(&acc.dir, name) }                                    // `src::Widget`
}
```
`inline namespace v1` is one ns_path segment. visit_type records `local_types.entry(join(&scope.ns_path, name)).or_insert((id, qname))` (first declaration wins). Nav parents and DEFINES / CONTAINS edges are unchanged (MODULE / PACKAGE -> type, type -> method): only qnames move (LB.7d's precedent). Inline methods keep `<type qname>::<name>`; enums follow type_qname. Unqualified free functions keep `<parent_qname>::<name>`. LB.10a's bodiless-specifier rule means only definitions reach type_qname, so a forward declaration in another header never shares (and pollutes) the real type's qname.
Out-of-line (visit_function when `name.rsplit_once("::")` is Some((q, m))):
```rust
// C++ looks a qualified definition's scope up from its own namespace outward (prefixes of `a::b`: `a::b`, `a`, "").
let local = prefixes(&scope.ns_path).find_map(|p| acc.local_types.get(&join(p, q)).cloned());
match local {
    // In-file: final. METHOD `{tq}::{m}`, nav name m, nav parent the type, DEFINES type -> method.
    Some((tid, tq)) => ..,
    // Provisional (LB.10c binds / renames): METHOD at the header rule's qname, nav name `q::m` (LB.10c's candidate
    // marker), nav parent + DEFINES from the lexical scope - HEAD's parent structure.
    None => {
        let full = join(&scope.ns_path, q);
        let owner = if full.contains("::") { full } else { join(&acc.dir, &full) };
        ..  // METHOD `{owner}::{m}`
    }
}
```
The body's CallSites are collected from the method id in both cases (collect_calls_in, unchanged), so SelfMethod calls in an in-file-bound member resolve through enclosing_class_or_struct (graph/src/calls.rs) at graph build. The provisional METHOD kind is right for the common case (the qualifier names a class) and its qname equals the bound one whenever the class sits in the definition's directory (global namespace) or namespace; LB.10c fixes the rest (a namespace-qualified free function `void shop::init() {}` provisionally reads METHOD `src::shop::init`). extract_func_name: when the node is a reference_declarator, continue into its first named child. Template definitions stay unvisited (template_declaration, as at HEAD), so a qualifier never carries template arguments here.
Marker (GLIA_QNAME_DEBUG, LB.2's OnceLock precedent), per file with >= 1 type or out-of-line member: `[qname] c_cpp: {h} header types scoped ({n} namespace, {d} directory), {l} file-local types kept, {o} out-of-line members ({b} bound in-file, {p} provisional) file={file_rel}`.
