HEAD parsers/code/extractors/src/data_entities.rs first_quoted_string (:336) returns the FIRST `'`, `"` or backtick literal ANYWHERE in the text after a needle - skipping identifiers, code and newlines to reach it - and the literal itself may span lines. Its callers (repo-graph impact --backward on first_quoted_string: scan_orm_table_decls :313, scan_mongoose_models :366, scan_dynamodb_tables :389, scan_collection_calls :440, scan_beanie_documents :479) pass the text after `__tablename__` / `db_table` (via `after.find('=')`, any distance away), `mongoose.model(` / `models.model(`, `TableName:` / `TableName =` / `TableName=` / `dynamodb.Table(`, `.collection(`, and the beanie `name` word inside a 256-byte window after `class Settings:`. The emit funnel's is_noise_entity_name (:243) rejects only empty, numeric and a keyword list.
MEASURED ON HEAD (debug CLI json): the glia self-build mints 6 data_entity:nosql:* nodes that are not names, all CONTAINed by parsers::code::extractors::src::data_entities (the scanner's own source): `<Name>` (the module doc's `mongoose.model('<Name>', ...)`), `, ` (the needle tables `["mongoose.model(", "models.model("]` / `["TableName:", "TableName =", ...]`), `...` (a doc comment `TableName: '...'`), and three multi-line names from `.collection(` in its code and tests (`) {
        let pos = search_from + rel; ...`, `);
    }

    #[test]
    fn firestore_and_mongo_collection_calls() { ...`, `
        // matches but `). quokka-stack, lapse, neuropil, repo-graph and the 16 glia-eval framework samples: no malformed DATA_ENTITY name (they hold no needle tables).
The location bug also hits real code shapes, reproduced in the probe fixture: `mongoose.model(modelName, schema)` takes a later unrelated string (nosql:Registry), `TableName: process.env.ORDERS_TABLE` takes an Item attribute value (nosql:pending - the environment-named table is the usual AWS shape), `@declared_attr def __tablename__(cls): return ...` takes a constant further down (sql:audit), beanie `name = collection_name()` takes the next field's literal (nosql:strict).
Probe fixture data-entity-literal-shape graded on HEAD (installed wheel): nodes 4/4, ACCESSES_DATA 2/2, FORBID VIOLATIONS 5.
LG.3b (W10) rewrites scan_collection_calls (argument 1 must be a literal or nameof) and the SQL scan; it does not touch mongoose / TableName / dynamodb.Table / __tablename__ / db_table / beanie, which still call first_quoted_string - the item's 'rest'. LE.4a leaves these declarations at module level (no access site), so nothing downstream re-reads them.

packets.implementation:
(1) LITERAL READERS (~45 LOC). `leading_literal(s)`: skip ASCII whitespace (space, tab, , 
); the next byte must be `'`, `"` or a backtick, else NotLiteral; scan bytes for the same quote byte - a `
`, ``, a backslash or end of input first -> Malformed; else Lit(&s[a..b]) with a and b at ASCII quote bytes (char-safe). A Python triple quote reads as an empty literal -> Malformed; an f-string / template starts with a letter or its body fails (3). `inline_literal(s)`: the same after skipping only spaces and tabs (an assignment's value is on its line). first_quoted_string is deleted; no caller keeps 'first quote anywhere'.
(2) SCANNERS (~70 LOC). scan_mongoose_models: `leading_literal(after_needle)`. scan_dynamodb_tables: the three key needles keep HEAD's prev-byte word boundary and use inline_literal; `dynamodb.Table(` uses leading_literal. scan_orm_table_decls: needle matching unchanged (a `my_db_table = "x"` variable still reads x, as at HEAD - usually a table name); after it skip spaces/tabs, an optional `:` + annotation up to `=` on the same line, then `=` not followed by `=`, then inline_literal; anything else (`def __tablename__(cls):`) -> no name. scan_beanie_documents: keep LA.25a's snapped 256-byte bound; compute the indentation of the `class Settings:` line; walk the following lines inside the bound, skipping blank lines, stopping at the first line not indented deeper; a line whose trimmed text starts with the word `name` followed by optional spaces, an optional `: <annotation>`, and `=` takes inline_literal of the rest; other lines are skipped (so `name = collection_name()` yields nothing and a later field's literal is never read). scan_collection_calls (LG.3b's rewrite): argument 1 = leading_literal(after the `(`) or LG.3b's `nameof(Ident)` -> Ident; NotLiteral / Malformed -> no node (a literal that does not start the argument or does not close on its line never names a collection). This replaces whatever literal read LG.3b used, so no caller of first_quoted_string remains and the function is deleted.
(3) EMIT FUNNEL (~15 LOC). `fn entity_shaped(name: &str) -> bool`: 1..=128 bytes; first char `char::is_alphanumeric` or `_`; every char `char::is_alphanumeric` or one of `_ - . /` (Mongo `system.users`, DynamoDB `orders-v2`, Firestore `users/abc/orders`; non-ASCII collection names such as `usuários` pass, as LA.41 does for event names). is_noise_entity_name returns true when !entity_shaped - one gate for every scanner and flavor (SQL names from canonical_sql_name and Cypher labels are already [A-Za-z0-9_], so they are unaffected; LG.3b's nameof / literal collection names and A13.9's DDL names pass).
